The door the candidates were turned away at

Run 567's beacon said w8m3c2r0 OSDictionary: the matching was given two
candidates, they are dictionaries, and they were not turned away before the
loop's body.  So they went in and were turned away inside it -- and the
reasons for that live in NIO_DROP, on the panel, once.

A mark written once is gone by the time the console text catches up with
it, so the reason rides with the beacon now: d is the reason of the last
door the candidates were turned away at, zero when none has been, and the
class after it is the personality that was turned away.  The numbers are
the matching's own:

  1  the candidate is a dext and dexts are off
  2  a dext relaunch is needed and the budget is spent
  3  the match category was consumed by another client
  4  the properties could not be copied
  5  the nub does not match the personality
  6  the kext that holds the personality is not loaded
  7  the client is being terminated for replacement
  8  the match category was consumed
  9  the personality is not the one being rematched
